      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225552",
      ":question/problem": "A total of $N = 345$ customers of an insurance company took out a particular policy. In a random sample of $n = 120$ of these customers, $87$ declared they were satisfied with the company's service.\n\nFind a $95%$ confidence interval for the population proportion $p$ of customers who are satisfied with the service.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\nThe required confidence interval is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
