      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251431",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/39/391592a451e201eb026c1df951319c7ba6915d9650a6b31e8d7e7ef52d932e1a.png)\n\nA total of $N = 800$ customers of a company used a delivery service. In a random sample of $n = 200$ of these customers, a proportion of $p^(^) = 0.68$ declared they were satisfied with the delivery service.\n\nFind a $90%$ confidence interval for the population proportion $p$ of customers who are satisfied with the delivery service.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.645) = 0.05$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
